    <name>🧭 LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 12:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (NOMADS)<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260925-t16z-mslma-anl<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 01:31 PM EDT<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (hourly HRRR cycle)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/surface_pressure/legend.png?v=hrrr-hrrr.20260925-t16z-mslma-anl" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Sea-level pressure (hPa, HRRR analysis, fixed absolute scale): <b>LOWEST 980</b> dark-blue deep low &rarr; <b>1000</b> cyan &rarr; <b>1006</b> green &rarr; <b>AVERAGE 1013.25</b> yellow middle &rarr; <b>1017</b> orange &rarr; <b>1023</b> red &rarr; <b>1029</b> magenta &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 1040</b> dark-purple. Same pressure always shows the same color; the everyday average sits in the middle. Current basin range: <b>1018-1029 hPa</b> (above average (high)).</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km MSLMA mean sea-level pressure analysis (hourly cycles)<br/><a href="https://rapidrefresh.noaa.gov/hrrr">https://rapidrefresh.noaa.gov/hrrr</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE SURFACE PRESSURE</h2><p>Hourly HRRR sea-level pressure analysis over the Great Lakes basin in hPa. The everyday average (1013.25 hPa) is the middle color so lows and highs read as departures from normal at a glance.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/surface_pressure/legend.png?v=hrrr-hrrr.20260925-t16z-mslma-anl" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Sea-level pressure (hPa, HRRR analysis, fixed absolute scale): <b>LOWEST 980</b> dark-blue deep low &rarr; <b>1000</b> cyan &rarr; <b>1006</b> green &rarr; <b>AVERAGE 1013.25</b> yellow middle &rarr; <b>1017</b> orange &rarr; <b>1023</b> red &rarr; <b>1029</b> magenta &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 1040</b> dark-purple. Same pressure always shows the same color; the everyday average sits in the middle. Current basin range: <b>1018-1029 hPa</b> (above average (high)).</p><p><b>Units:</b> hPa (hectopascals, sea-level)<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km MSLMA mean sea-level pressure analysis (hourly cycles)<br/><b>Update:</b> HRRR hourly cycles<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 12:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> hrrr-hrrr.20260925-t16z-mslma-anl<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-25 01:31 PM EDT<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://rapidrefresh.noaa.gov/hrrr">NOAA HRRR</a></p>]]></description>
